    "q-48560": {
      "dom_id": "step-q48560",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ when $f(x)={sin}^{2}⁡x.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we express\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we see that $f(x)$ can be expressed as the composite function\n\n$$\nf={u}^{2},\\,u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=2u\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =2u\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
