    "q-51025": {
      "dom_id": "step-q51025",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Calculate the derivative of $y=2\\operatorname{sec}⁡(6x-2).$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=2\\operatorname{sec}⁡u,\\,u=6x-2.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=2\\operatorname{sec}⁡u\\operatorname{tan}⁡u,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=6.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sec}⁡u\\operatorname{tan}⁡u\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =12\\operatorname{sec}⁡u\\operatorname{tan}⁡u \\\\  & =12\\operatorname{sec}⁡(6x-2)\\operatorname{tan}⁡(6x-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
